  "question": {
    "text": "If a curve passes through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and has slope of the tangent at any point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> on it as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math>, then the curve also passes through the point",
